3. The appellant contended that on 19th September, 2011 he was driving his Maruti Wagon-R car from Bangalore to Tumakuru and at 9.00 pm when he reached near Hosanijagal Gate, a Canter lorry bearing registration No.MH 04 DK 5126 NC: 2023:KHC:20823 came from behind in a rash and negligent manner and dashed against the vehicle of the appellant causing accident and the vehicle of the appellant/petitioner had sustained damages as below:
1. Bonnet damaged at left side;
2. Left Head light indicators damaged;
3. Left fender front door damaged;
4. Wind screen glass broken;
5. top roof damaged at front;
6. Dash board damaged.
4. After the police inspection, the vehicle was towed to the service centre and the Engineer estimated the cost and caused repairs; and it took about three months for repair of the car and the repair

Consequently, I pass the following:
NC: 2023:KHC:20823 ORDER 1. Appeal is allowed in part;
2.

